+a receiving-environment check. Optional `filesystem_policy` supports
+`include_workdir`, absolute `read_only` paths and absolute `read_write` paths.
+Optional `landlock.compatibility` accepts `best_effort` or `hard_requirement`.
+Optional `process` requires both `run_as_user` and `run_as_group`. These settings
+are translated by the same adapter for invocation-owned and retained environments.
+This is not the full OpenShell policy YAML schema: richer network fields such as
+HTTP method/path rules are rejected. The gateway validates backend semantics.
+
+A supplied policy replaces the image policy; it is not an overlay. Include the
+filesystem, process and Landlock settings needed by the selected image when
+customizing its network rules. Omitting policy preserves the image's policy.
+A pre-existing sandbox retains its own policy; pairing `sandbox_id` with `policy`
+is rejected before client allocation rather than silently ignoring the policy.
 
